        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/queens-domain-header_not_gta2.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>Where to start with Queen's Domain? It's tempting to begin with King's Field; after all, FromSoftware's seminal first-person action-RPG is an explicit inspiration for developer Freshly Baked Games. But 40 hours later, it feels like so much more. It's equally tempting to invoke another FromSoftware game: Dark Souls. Queen's Domain owes an obvious debt to that game's celebrated level design: the dazzling interconnectedness of its vertiginous world. But that's not quite right either. The deeper you delve, the more there's something of the spirit of The Legend of Zelda, a touch of Metroidvania too. Until finally you concede that Queen's Domain, with its remarkable world of densely packed secrets, is very much its own.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/queens-domain-review\">Read more</a></p>",
